\newlabel{fig:03-overlap}{{3.8}{51}{Overlapping observations. Each observation in a regression of five-year returns covers 60 months, and each starts one month after the last. Consecutive observations share 59 of their 60 months, so they carry almost the same information}{figure.caption.22}{}}
