\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.9}{\ignorespaces Simulated stock price paths from two MCMC algorithms, each showing 1,000 paths over 200 trading days from a starting price of \$100 (horizontal line). (a)~With Gibbs sampling, each day's return is drawn independently, and the paths spread evenly around the starting price. (b)~With the Metropolis--Hastings algorithm, each day's return depends on the previous day's, and a few paths rise far above the rest. Note the different vertical scales. Source: Kuo (2025), Figures 14.6 and 14.10.}}{54}{figure.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:03-mcmc-paths}{{3.9}{54}{Simulated stock price paths from two MCMC algorithms, each showing 1,000 paths over 200 trading days from a starting price of \$100 (horizontal line). (a)~With Gibbs sampling, each day's return is drawn independently, and the paths spread evenly around the starting price. (b)~With the Metropolis--Hastings algorithm, each day's return depends on the previous day's, and a few paths rise far above the rest. Note the different vertical scales. Source: Kuo (2025), Figures 14.6 and 14.10}{figure.caption.24}{}}
